1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,840
Hello to schw reproduce

2
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:29,980
Mr. Renogu

3
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:38,740
Mr. Rengoku?

4
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,320
Mr. Rengoku!

5
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:47,740
I...

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:52,240
I will see my duty fulfilled!

7
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:56,340
No matter what it takes, no one shall die here!

8
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:57,640
Flame breathing.

9
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,560
Esoteric art!

10
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,840
Set your heart ablaze.

11
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:17,980
Mr. Rengoku!

12
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:19,120
No!

13
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:41,280
Set your heart ablaze.

14
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,400
Mr. Rengoku?

15
00:01:47,980 --> 00:02:17,960
Thank you.

16
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:47,960
Thank you.

17
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:49,820
Mr. Rengoku.

18
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:51,700
Mr. Rengoku.

19
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,700
Mr. Rengoku.

20
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,340
Stop that train, will ya?

21
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:02,340
And you, snap out of it and get back on your feet!

22
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,280
We all have to train!

23
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:06,040
You hear me?

24
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:36,020
You hear me?

25
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:47,520
Is that so?

26
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:49,820
Tanjiro said that.

27
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:59,380
I'm not done with you, coward!

28
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,100
Turn and face me!

29
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:05,840
Don't forget that the Demon Slayer Corps is always fighting you demons in the dead of night!

30
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,340
Where you have the advantage!

31
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,400
Don't run away, you bastard!

32
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,560
You're a coward!

33
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:11,600
You're a coward!

34
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,540
A coward!

35
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:24,420
Then our newfound duty is to carry on his will.

36
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:30,860
Now, it's a resource.

37
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:37,320
No one was trapped!

38
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:39,860
You're a coward!

39
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:40,820
You're a coward!

40
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:42,060
Look wee!

41
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:42,960
You're a coward!

42
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:43,260
All right!

43
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:43,940
There is no joy!

44
00:04:43,940 --> 00:05:13,920
We'll be right back.

45
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:43,920
We'll be right back.

46
00:05:43,940 --> 00:06:13,920
We'll be right back.

47
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:43,920
We'll be right back.

48
00:06:43,920 --> 00:07:13,900
We'll be right back.

49
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:16,580
I may have that boy take over my business one day.

50
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:19,620
I'd be lying if I said I weren't jealous.

51
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,180
I wish I could trade our useless son for him.

52
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:27,180
He's a fine young lad, there's no doubt.

53
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:35,160
That being said, the poor boy suffers from a rare skin disease, so he can't go outside during the day.

54
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,240
Oh dear, I'm so sorry.

55
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:43,320
I'm hoping we can figure out a way to develop a miracle elixir for him over at my company.

56
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,940
The sooner the better.

57
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:58,880
Reporting in as you requested, Lord Muzan.

58
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:05,880
Were you able to find what I asked for?

59
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:09,960
I looked into it, but came up empty-handed.

60
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:12,420
I couldn't find the blue spider lily.

61
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:16,560
There wasn't even a trace of its existence.

62
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:20,140
And?

63
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:24,440
I will try to live up to your expectations.

64
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,660
Forgive my unworthy efforts.

65
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:31,480
But as you ordered, I was able to eliminate one of the Hashira.

66
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,520
Rest easy knowing that much.

67
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:41,640
It seems like you have the wrong idea about how things work here, Akaza.

68
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:43,500
I'm curious.

69
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:49,200
Did you expect praise?

70
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:52,620
All you did was dispose of a mere cockroach.

71
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:56,800
A demon beating a human is an underwhelming conclusion.

72
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:01,940
What I want is for the Demon Slayer core to be wiped out.

73
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,960
Squeeze the life out of every last one of them.

74
00:09:07,300 --> 00:09:09,860
And never let another one enter my line of sight again.

75
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:13,720
It's hardly a complicated task.

76
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:16,740
And yet I am still waiting for it to happen.

77
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:18,520
Now what do you make of that?

78
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:25,440
You return here boasting of your infantile triumph over a Hashira.

79
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:28,960
All the while, three other Demon Slayers survived the confrontation.

80
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,120
Why did you not kill them when you had the chance?

81
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:36,940
And after I made a point of sending you to that location because you happened to be nearby.

82
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:39,580
Akaza.

83
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,280
Akaza.

84
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,040
Akaza.

85
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:47,260
Akaza!

86
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,000
You have disappointed me so.

87
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:57,200
To think you suffered a blow by someone who isn't even a Hashira.

88
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:00,380
Ah, how far you have fallen, Upper Three.

89
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:06,980
You're dismissed.

90
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,120
What's all the commotion up here?

91
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:17,560
Are you alright?

92
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:34,960
You coward!

93
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:52,900
Make no mistake.

94
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,840
I'll remember your face.

95
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,740
And when we meet again,

96
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,800
I'm going to save her tearing you limb from limb.

97
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:29,220
I'm sorry.

98
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:48,260
I never thought I'd live to see the day

99
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:50,720
where even Tanjiro couldn't bring himself to smile.

100
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,080
It makes sense, though.

101
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:58,260
We were powerless compared to Mr. Rengoku.

102
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,040
And even he found himself at death's door.

103
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:04,200
I don't blame him.

104
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:05,860
I would break anyone.

105
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,460
I mean, just look at Inosuke.

106
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,900
I didn't even know he could cry.

107
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,680
He must have been so frustrated

108
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:18,600
that his burning rage turned to helpless tears.

109
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:23,460
Even so, there's no point in cowering forever.

110
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:26,980
The strong get back up on their feet time and time again.

111
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:30,020
I know Mr. Rengoku was that way.

112
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,500
I could hear that in him.

113
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,960
He was a little odd at times,

114
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:37,440
but his heart was strong and kind.

115
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:40,500
Tanjiro!

116
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,460
I snagged his bean paste buns.

117
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:43,180
Let's eat!

118
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,180
Help!

119
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:46,280
Mr. Tanjiro has gone missing!

120
00:12:46,860 --> 00:12:47,700
Oh no!

121
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:48,960
Mr. Zenitsu!

122
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:50,360
I'm so sorry!

123
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:53,480
Don't worry about it.

124
00:12:53,860 --> 00:12:54,720
I'll be okay.

125
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:55,940
Eventually.

126
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:58,740
You look like you just got hit by a train.

127
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:01,060
Please forgive me, sir.

128
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,780
But Mr. Tanjiro can't be found!

129
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:04,740
Even worse!

130
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:07,400
His wounds haven't healed and he's training again!

131
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,040
Maybe Shinobu told him he should be resting in bed!

132
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:13,020
But he didn't listen and now we don't know what we should do!

133
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,160
So he's training with that stomach wound?

134
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,060
Is he dumb?

135
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:33,400
Mr. Rengoku's crow.

136
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:34,680
Thank you.

137
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:39,020
He's carrying out his master's will by guiding me to his house.

138
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:39,080
Thank you.

139
00:13:48,060 --> 00:14:02,420
Are you...

140
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,360
Senjuro?

141
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:03,460
Are you Senjuro?

142
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:14,920
I take it you know about Mr. Kyojiro?

143
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,140
I'm so sorry.

144
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:21,700
Before he died, he asked for some messages to be delivered to you and your father.

145
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,780
I've come to pass them on.

146
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,160
From my brother?

147
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:31,900
Thank you, but I'm already well aware of what happened to him.

148
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:33,880
What's wrong?

149
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:35,140
Your face...

150
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,220
It looks as pale as a ghost.

151
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,640
Knock it off!

152
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:44,000
Whatever message she left means nothing anyway!

153
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,880
Why would he become a swordsman when he had no talent to begin with?

154
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:50,640
It's no wonder he died!

155
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:51,980
He's worthless!

156
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,860
He was a fool of a son from the start!

157
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:01,060
A person's potential is determined the day they're born.

158
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:04,620
Only a mere handful have any talent.

159
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:07,400
The rest are just dregs of society.

160
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:11,220
You're either born a genius or someday killed by one!

161
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,820
It's clear which one Kyojiro was.

162
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:18,640
He had no future to begin with.

163
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,860
No surprise he got killed.

164
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:24,060
Give me a break.

165
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:26,260
The funeral is over, Senjuro.

166
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:29,760
It's high time you move on with your damn life!

167
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:33,000
Just a moment.

168
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,680
Don't you think you're being a bit too harsh?

169
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,560
Please show some respect for your son!

170
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,240
And just who the hell are you?

171
00:15:42,100 --> 00:15:43,040
Answer me!

172
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,200
Or get off of my property!

173
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:48,220
I'm with the Demon Slayer Corps!

174
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:54,180
You're what?

175
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,500
I get it now.

176
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,200
That means...

177
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,660
You're a sun-breathing user, aren't you?

178
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,260
Am I right?

179
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:03,940
Sun-breathing?

180
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,960
What do you mean by that?

181
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:12,960
He's fast!

182
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:15,200
And knows where no amateur moves!

183
00:16:15,780 --> 00:16:16,180
Father!

184
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:17,520
Please stop!

185
00:16:18,040 --> 00:16:19,480
Take a good look at his face!

186
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:21,220
Can't you see he's in pain?

187
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:22,520
Keep your mouth shut!

188
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,980
Don't you dare lay a hand on him, you monster!

189
00:16:27,980 --> 00:16:37,500
Why are you acting so hostile like this in the first place?

190
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:40,620
Insulting your own child who lost his life?

191
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,340
And striking your son?

192
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:44,100
What's the matter with you?

193
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:46,980
Despicable.

194
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:51,080
You intend to mock us after everything we've been through!

195
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:53,280
What makes you say that?

196
00:16:53,700 --> 00:16:55,320
I don't know what you're talking about!

197
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:56,960
I'm here to help!

198
00:16:56,960 --> 00:17:00,500
A sun-breathing user would never help people like us!

199
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,940
I know all about those earrings of yours!

200
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,020
It was in that book!

201
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,080
Sun-breathing sounds familiar!

202
00:17:09,720 --> 00:17:11,740
Is he talking about Hinokami Kagura?

203
00:17:12,580 --> 00:17:13,960
The sun-breathing technique...

204
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:17,940
Not only is it the first one ever to be created,

205
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,400
it's the most powerful one as well!

206
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:25,060
Every technique, no matter how diverse, came from sun-breathing!

207
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:31,360
Which means all the others are just cheap imitations of sun-breathing!

208
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:35,900
They can try to copy the original, but they'll never be as powerful!

209
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,160
Fire!

210
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:37,980
Water!

211
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:38,840
Wind!

212
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,040
All of them!

213
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:42,400
What does he mean?

214
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:45,600
We've always been charcoal burners!

215
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:47,800
It's in our blood!

216
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:50,040
Sun-breathing...

217
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,040
Hinokami Kagura...

218
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:53,580
No...

219
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:55,580
No...

220
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:57,580
Never mind all that...

221
00:17:57,580 --> 00:18:01,580
There's something more important...

222
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,960
Don't get cocky just because you're a sun-breathing user!

223
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:07,320
I can still put you in your place, boy!

224
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:13,200
How can I feel cocky after all that's happened?

225
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:17,740
I would give anything at all for strength like that, but I'm burdened by my own weakness!

226
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:18,840
You bastard!

227
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,200
So shut up!

228
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:22,300
He's powerful!

229
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:22,960
Be careful!

230
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,580
How dare you badmouth Mr. Rengoku!

231
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:26,880
You monster!

232
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:28,760
Need the former Hashira!

233
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:32,660
Please, father!

234
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:34,380
Have mercy!

235
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:35,760
Why then...

236
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:39,760
If Hinokami Kagura is a sun-breathing technique...

237
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,760
Then that day...

238
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:47,580
Why wasn't I strong enough to save him?

239
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:51,820
Why?

240
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:53,860
Why?

241
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,920
Why couldn't I save him?

242
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:13,100
I feel like I've made a grave mistake.

243
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,300
Please, sir.

244
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:20,440
Have some tea.

245
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,140
Oh, thank you very much.

246
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,580
I hope you can forgive me...

247
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:28,940
For head-butting your father and all.

248
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,020
He's okay, right?

249
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:32,980
Oh, yeah.

250
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:33,780
He'll be fine.

251
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:35,580
I mean, after all...

252
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,100
He's back to getting sake already.

253
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:40,660
What a relief.

254
00:19:41,620 --> 00:19:42,900
You have my thanks.

255
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:44,560
Huh?

256
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:47,480
For standing up to him.

257
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,040
I was too scared to.

258
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,260
Even when he badmouthed my brother like that.

259
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:58,820
Tell me.

260
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:01,440
What were my brother's last moments like?

261
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:11,640
I see.

262
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,340
So he was brave to the end.

263
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:18,000
Thank you for sharing.

264
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:21,940
Please, don't thank me.

265
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:24,300
Instead, forgive me.

266
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:25,840
I wasn't enough.

267
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,740
There's no need to blame yourself.

268
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,680
It's not your fault.

269
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:36,340
And he knows that, too.

270
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:46,540
What you said reminded me of something in a book my father often read.

271
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:51,080
I'm fairly certain this is it.

272
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:56,280
Thank you very much.

273
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,980
Let me know if what you're looking for is in those pages.

274
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:05,060
What?

275
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:06,800
Look at this.

276
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:18,700
What happened?

277
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,540
